@@ -15,3 +15,39 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+The sign-up form uses the server-side `api/signup` endpoint with Twilio Verify.
+Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and
+`TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID` in the server process environment (see `.env.example`).
+Configure your Verify service for **6-digit SMS codes** and enable Fraud Guard
+and appropriate provider rate limits before exposing SMS delivery publicly.
+Credentials and verification codes are never returned to the browser or logged.
+An absent configuration returns a visible service-unavailable message; no mock
+verification or test passcode is enabled.
+
+Account registration runs only after Twilio returns `approved`. A signed,
+HttpOnly, same-site cookie binds the verification session to the phone number
+and account details for ten minutes. Registration still uses the existing
+external registration API; that API must independently enforce phone verification
+if other clients can call it directly. The external API owns persistent account
+and phone storage.
+
+For automatic SMS extraction, serve the page over HTTPS and configure the
+Twilio Verify SMS template to end with the actual website hostname and code:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 123456.
+
+@example.com #123456
+```
+
+Replace the hostname and code with your actual hostname and template code
+variable. See [WebOTP SMS formatting](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp)
+and [Twilio verification templates](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api/templates).
+The form supports WebOTP on compatible browsers, `autocomplete="one-time-code"`
+on supporting platforms, and manual entry or paste everywhere. Autofill never
+submits the account without the user's explicit action.
+
+Run `pnpm test:signup` for the production build and mocked-provider verification tests.
